+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+A task can only be referred to by its title, and a rename changes the title. The app needs a stable
+reference that survives renames.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Each task gets an `id`: a string no other task of the list has, and which never changes.
+- `add` returns the task with its `id`.
+- The list gets `get(id)`, returning a `Result<Task>` like the other methods.
+- `find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag` and `remove` accept a task's id as well as its title.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-list`: how tasks are identified and looked up in the task list (no spec exists yet for the list).
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/domain/task.ts`: `Task` gains `id`.
+- `src/domain/list.ts`: id assignment, `get`, id-or-title lookup.
+- `test/list.test.ts`: new tests. No new dependency.
